    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "Note",
      "title": "Read me",
      "pos": [
        40,
        340
      ],
      "size": [
        700,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Dormouse pixel-art generator. Docs: tools/art/README.md and tools/art/PROMPTS.md.\n\n* Width and height must be multiples of 16. PixelArtRedmond draws one fake pixel per 16x16 block, aligned to the top-left corner, so the true sprite size is width/16 x height/16.\n  - 768 x 768 -> 48x48 avatar canvas (seated figure ~28 px tall)\n  - 1024 x 1024 -> 64x64\n  - 1344 x 768 -> 84x48 wide scene\n  - 2048 x 1152 -> 128x72 (largest tested)\n* Keep the seed FIXED while iterating. To explore, change the seed by hand, one at a time. Every saved PNG embeds this whole graph, including the seed: drag it back onto the canvas to reproduce it.\n* Keep 'Pixel Art, PixArFK,' at the start of the positive prompt. Those are the LoRA's trigger words.\n* Output lands in /var/lib/comfyui/output/dormouse/. Then downsample and quantize: see README.md."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
